# Styling Conventions

## Tailwind CSS v4 Only

All styles go in Tailwind utility classes on the JSX element. Do not create new `.css` files or `<style>` tags.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
<div className="flex items-center gap-4 bg-black/20 border border-border rounded-lg p-6">

// ❌ BAD — no new CSS files or inline style objects for layout
<div style={{ display: 'flex', gap: '16px' }}>
```

## Design Tokens

Defined in `src/index.css` under `@theme` and available as Tailwind classes:

| Token | Class | Value |
|---|---|---|
| `--color-pink` | `bg-pink`, `text-pink`, `border-pink` | `#ff008c` |
| `--color-pink-hover` | `hover:bg-pink-hover` | `#e6007d` |
| `--color-cyan` | `text-cyan` | `#2bffed` |
| `--color-purple` | `text-purple` | `#9b84ff` |
| `--color-magenta` | `text-magenta` | `#ff00bf` |
| `--color-bg` | `bg-bg` | `#000000` |
| `--color-border` | `border-border` | `rgba(255,255,255,0.18)` |
| `--color-border-light` | `border-border-light` | `rgba(255,255,255,0.08)` |

Always use these tokens rather than raw hex values.

## Fluid/Clamp Sizing

For sizes that should scale between breakpoints, use CSS `clamp()` via arbitrary values:

```tsx
<h1 className="text-[clamp(32px,2.5vw,48px)]">
```

## Pointer Events

The LiquidEther background sits at `z-index: 0`. Page content is at `z-index: 10`. The layout uses `pointer-events: none` on containers that should pass mouse events through to the background, and `pointer-events: auto` on interactive elements.

- Containers/sections that should be transparent to mouse: `pointer-events-none`
- Buttons, links, inputs, interactive cards: `pointer-events-auto`

## Card / Panel Pattern

Consistent border style for cards and floating panels:

```tsx
<div className="border-2 border-border rounded-lg bg-black/20 p-6">
```

For highlighted/active cards (e.g. Pro plan), use `border-pink` instead.

## Gradient Text

```tsx
<span className="bg-gradient-to-r from-cyan via-purple to-magenta bg-clip-text text-transparent">
  Nice Touch
</span>
```
